#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:5
#: 6e29a28503004e9da1004721889b2996
msgid "Using DO_LAND_START"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:7
#: 9495a9a1f4b84a61a73f54fec289ed89
msgid "The :ref:`DO_LAND_START <mav_cmd_do_land_start>` mission item can be used for two purposes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:9
#: a62532ce5f5749318a17792b8bfbd403
msgid "In Plane, to provide an automatic re-attempt for an aborted NAV_LAND autolanding in a mission. (See :ref:`aborting-autolanding`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:10
#: e9a8114f221f4cd39ea215cef026faa2
msgid "To provide an automatic landing sequence for RTLs in Plane or as a failsafe action in Copter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:12
#: c50e459aec6e455eb92c490131770697
msgid "in Rover, it can be used, but only via Scripting call to start the landing sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:15
#: f9fa487699f64b4db8103665171ed711
msgid "To trigger an automatic landing as part of an RTL(return to launch) you need to do two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:17
#: b89f31cc82424adea0587ce96aaa4c9d
msgid "add a :ref:`DO_LAND_START <mav_cmd_do_land_start>` mission item to your mission, just before the start of your landing sequence which sets up the approach waypoints and ends with a NAV_LAND item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:18
#: 4c6198b4caf545cca6d4ad035b32c9e9
msgid "set the :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND <RTL_AUTOLAND>` parameter to 1 or 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:20
#: 0771732bebf345b49d7e6f3a17aff932
msgid "The exact behaviour depends on the :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` value: -  If :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` = 1, then the plane will first RTL as normal, then when it starts circling the return point (home or a rally point) it will then switch to the AUTO mission after the ``DO_LAND_START`` -  If :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` = 2, then the plane will bypass the RTL completely and go straight to the landing sequence after the ``DO_LAND_START``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:24
#: 685ccf1292b54a1da8009dce22483365
msgid "the \"landing sequence\" whose start is the ``DO_LAND_START`` marker, does not actually have to include a landing! it can be any sequence of valid mission commands. For example, flying to a location, and changing to an indefinite VTOL loiter (applies only to a QuadPlane, obviously)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:26
#: ba392186a9b740ea846ded7a0ae9a3da
msgid "ArduPilot checks to see if there is a ``DO_LAND_START`` mission items before arming, and :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` is set to 0. If so, a pre-arm failure condition will prevent arming. If it is desired to use a ``DO_LAND_START`` only for aborted autolandings and not as an RTL action override, then set :ref:`RTL_AUTOLAND<RTL_AUTOLAND>` = 3, to allow arming. Its use for an aborted autolanding is explained in :ref:`aborting-autolanding`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:28
#: 89be628e501e44a8a395d1f0acf08455
msgid "if you execute an RTL due to a battery failsafe and the :ref:`MIS_OPTIONS<MIS_OPTIONS>` bit 1 (Use distance to land) is set, then if continuing the mission results in a closer landing point, then the mission will proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:33
#: 2a581b1faaf64022b7d946e0cd62afa1
msgid "You can optionally include more than one ``DO_LAND_START`` mission item in your mission. If that is done then the latitude/longitude/altitude of the ``DO_LAND_START`` mission items is used to choose which landing sequence to use. The ``DO_LAND_START`` closest to the current location in all three dimensions is used. This can be useful if you have multiple landing sequences for different wind conditions or different areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-do-land-start.rst:35
#: 269fecd61242419ca62e620fea263b49
msgid "If you are already in a landing sequence (NAV_LAND or DO_START_LAND sequence), then it will continue."
msgstr ""
